The chat worker's per-caller quota is implemented in `crates/coder/src/relay/quota.rs` (`coder::relay::quota`) (crates/coder/src/relay/quota.rs:1-14; docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:58-59).

Under its deployed configuration, the limits are:
- 6 jobs per caller key in any 60 seconds (docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:63);
- 40 jobs per caller key per UTC day (docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:64);
- 3,000 jobs per UTC day across every caller combined (docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:65);
- a maximum request ciphertext size of 96 KiB (docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:66);
- at most 8 jobs at once (docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:67).

Sources, as of commit e1d499def7: crates/coder/src/relay/quota.rs:1-14, docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:58-59, docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:63, docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:64, docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:65, docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:66, docs/deployment/chat-worker.md:67
